* Founding Machine Learning Engineer (Recommendations \+ GenAI)
**Founding Machine Learning Engineer (Recommendations \+ GenAI)**
=================================================================

We’re hiring a Founding Machine Learning Engineer to design and build the core intelligence behind everything we create.

Remote London Limassol Tbilisi Yerevan
**Are you ready to take your Machine Learning skills to the next level?**



We are hiring a Founding Machine Learning Engineer to own the intelligence layer of our products. You will design, build, and improve the models and decision systems behind recommendations, ranking, personalisation, retrieval, agent behaviour, and selected predictive analytics use cases. You will work directly with the founders to turn ambiguous product ideas into production systems that create measurable customer value. In a team of our size, this is an end\-to\-end role: you may touch data exploration, modelling, evaluation, experimentation, and production iteration in the same week.


**This is not a pure research role.** We care about people who can move from data and hypotheses to shipped systems and business impact.


**All you need is:**


* Strong foundations in machine learning, statistics, computer science, or a similar quantitative discipline;
* Experience building and shipping ML systems or intelligent product features in production or near\-production environments;
* Strong Python skills and comfort working across data, modelling, evaluation, and production collaboration;
* Good understanding of experimentation, model evaluation, feature engineering, data quality, and error analysis;
* Clear communication and the ability to work through messy, ambiguous product problems;
* High ownership, self\-direction, and a strong bias toward action;
* 5\+ years building and shipping ML systems or intelligent product features in production;
* Strong understanding of model evaluation, cross\-validation, feature engineering, and data quality challenges in real\-world environments;
* Experience working with large\-scale behavioural, transactional, or contextual data;
* Strong software engineering habits, including writing clean, testable, maintainable Python code.


**What would be an advantage:**


* Experience with recommendation systems, ranking, search, personalisation, or marketplace/feed optimisation;
* Experience with LLM applications, RAG, GenAI agents, prompt iteration, or evaluation of GenAI systems;
* Experience running A/B tests or online experiments;
* Experience working closely with product teams and translating user problems into ML solutions;
* Experience with real\-time ML, streaming features, low\-latency inference, or online learning;
* Experience with causal inference, uplift modelling, multi\-armed bandits, or other decision\-optimisation methods;
* Familiarity with cloud ML infrastructure, containerised deployment, and MLOps workflows;
* Experience in iGaming, fintech, e\-commerce, or another domain with large\-scale transactional and behavioural data;
* Experience with predictive analytics use cases such as segmentation, churn prevention, LTV modelling, or opportunity prioritisation.


**Your daily adventures will look like:**


* Design, build, and improve ML systems for recommendations, ranking, personalisation, retrieval, and GenAI workflows;
* Turn product goals into concrete ML problems, evaluation plans, experiments, and shipped features;
* Work with behavioural, transactional, contextual, and unstructured data to identify signals and improve model quality;
* Build offline evaluation frameworks and online experiments to measure relevance, quality, latency, cost, and business impact;
* Improve GenAI agent behaviour through better retrieval, context management, prompting, tool use, orchestration, and evaluation;
* Investigate failure modes, run error analysis, and make practical tradeoffs across quality, reliability, speed, and complexity;
* Partner closely with platform and backend engineers to deploy, monitor, and iterate on models in production;
* Help define how the company does ML: metrics, experimentation discipline, technical standards, and long\-term direction;
* Work with real\-time behavioural and transactional signals to improve recommendations, personalisation, and intelligent product behaviour;
* Contribute to predictive and insight\-driven ML use cases such as segmentation, churn prediction, recommendation measurement, and opportunity ranking;
* Write clean, testable Python and contribute reusable ML components and shared libraries used across the platform.


**What Success Looks Like in the First 6 Months:**


* You ship meaningful improvements to a recommendation, personalisation, or GenAI workflow used in production;
* You establish a practical evaluation framework for one or more core ML systems;
* You turn ambiguous product opportunities into clear experiments and sound technical decisions;
* You improve at least one metric that matters, such as relevance, task completion, conversion, retention, latency, or cost efficiency;
* You become a trusted owner who spots high\-leverage ML opportunities and drives them forward without needing detailed instruction;
* You help establish a repeatable approach to experimentation, model iteration, and production\-quality ML development.


**And this is how our interview process goes:**


* A 30\-minute interview with a member of our HR team to get to know you and your experience;
* A 1\-hour technical interview;
* A final interview to gauge your fit with our culture and working style.


**Sounds interesting? Do not hesitate to apply or contact us if you have any questions!**






**Advantages of Our Company**
-----------------------------

#### **Zero bureaucracy**

#### **Unlimited holidays**

#### **Medical insurance**

#### **Only top talent and top salaries**

#### **Challenging projects and tasks**

#### **Smartest colleagues in the industry**

**Our Principles**
------------------

### **Celebrate diversity**

Celebrate diversity


### **Innovation matters**

Innovation matters


### **Ambitious goals**

Ambitious goals

We are looking for
 **Generative AI Specialists** 
 (junior, intermediate, and middle\-senior profiles) to join BIP’s xTech Competence Centre, one of the largest Data Science communities in Europe.




 You will work on advanced AI projects for leading enterprise clients across multiple industries, developing
 **Generative AI** 
 solutions for real business use cases. You will be involved in initiatives leveraging pre\-trained models (such as LLMs) as well as training and fine\-tuning new models, especially in contexts with unstructured data (text, images, video, and audio).




 In addition, you will actively contribute to the internal AI Community through research, technology scouting, solution design, and business development initiatives.




**Mandatory Requirements**
* Master’s Degree in Computer Engineering, Mathematical Engineering, Computer Science, Statistics, or related STEM disciplines;
* Strong quantitative mindset and analytical skills;
* Passion and expertise in data exploration, data analysis, and model development;
* Strong knowledge of Statistics, Data Mining, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning;
* Solid programming experience in Python;
* Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git);
* Strong knowledge of relational databases and SQL programming;
* Knowledge of NoSQL databases (e.g., Elasticsearch, MongoDB, Redis);
* Experience with vector databases (e.g., ChromaDB, Qdrant, Pinecone);
* Experience using AI Cloud APIs from at least one major provider (Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure, AWS);
* Experience processing unstructured data;
* Strong knowledge of NLP and Computer Vision techniques (Text Categorization, Entity Extraction, Generation, Object Detection, Segmentation);
* Experience with Neural Networks, CNNs, and Transformers;
* Knowledge of Generative AI techniques and Large Language Models (LLMs);
* Experience in neural network training and fine\-tuning techniques (e.g., Super\-Convergence, PEFT, LoRA);
* Experience with major deep learning libraries (TensorFlow, PyTorch) and model repositories (Hugging Face);
* Knowledge of prompting techniques (one\-shot, few\-shot, chain\-of\-thought);
* Fluent professional proficiency in Spanish and English (mandatory).






**Nice to Have**
* Experience with containerization tools (Docker, Kubernetes);
* Experience developing and applying Generative AI models in industrial environments;
* Software development experience and strong knowledge of SDLC;
* Experience with data/model versioning frameworks (MLflow, DVC);
* Experience with generative networks for controlled content production (text, images, video);
* Experience building Search Engines, Entity Extraction systems, or Image Anomaly Detection solutions;
* Knowledge of Explainable AI models (SHAP, LIME, Anchors);
* Experience working in Agile frameworks (Scrum, Kanban);
* Knowledge of Data Engineering concepts (ETL/ELT pipelines, data modeling, distributed processing);
* Experience with big data frameworks such as Apache Spark;
* Hands\-on experience with Databricks (workspace management, notebooks, Delta Lake, MLflow integration);
* Experience designing scalable data architectures in cloud environments.






**Soft Skills**
* Strong consulting mindset;
* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;
* Client\-oriented and results\-driven;
* Teamwork attitude;
* Attention to detail and ability to work under deadlines.






**Why BIP?**
 Growth \& Learning




 Access to 300\+ courses on emerging technologies and business topics, personalized development programs, and continuous training initiatives to support your professional and personal growth.




 Flexibility \& Work\-Life Integration




 Hybrid working model with flexibility to balance remote and office work in agreement with your manager and project needs, plus initiatives supporting work\-life balance.




 Health \& Benefits




 Private health insurance, wellness platforms, meal vouchers, and an attractive benefits package.




 Family \& Parenthood




 Support for new parents, including enhanced parental leave benefits and dedicated initiatives during and after parental leave.




 Inclusion \& Values




 We promote uniqueness and equal opportunities for everyone. We are committed to creating an ethical, inclusive, and welcoming work environment.




**Next Steps**
 Once we receive your CV, we will carefully review your profile. If there is a match with this or other open positions within the Group, we will contact you to start our mutual introduction process.




 The selection process generally includes an HR interview, a technical interview with a Line Manager, and potentially a final interview with a Partner. The number and order of interviews may vary.




**About Us**
 Founded in 2003, BIP combines the historical excellence of management consulting with innovation and digitalization. Today we are more than 5,000 professionals across 13 countries, delivering over 4,500 projects worldwide.




 We support our clients in driving large\-scale impact through Digital Transformation, Data Science, Cybersecurity, Industry 4\.0, IoT, and disruptive technologies across all industries.




 We believe in excellence as our guiding principle and adopt an ethical and fair approach toward everyone who chooses to work with us, fostering an environment where people grow together through diverse expertise.




